/-!
# Morphisms of locally constant sheaves of modules

Let `J` be a Grothendieck topology on `C` and let `R` be a ring. A map `φ : F ⟶ G` of locally
constant sheaves of `R`-modules whose source is *of finite type* is, locally on the site, induced
by a homomorphism of `R`-modules: over every object `U` there is a covering `{X i ⟶ U}` and, on
each member, local trivializations `F|_{X i} ≅ A̲` and `G|_{X i} ≅ B̲` together with a homomorphism
`g : A ⟶ B` whose associated map of constant sheaves of modules is `φ|_{X i}`. This is Stacks
093S (3).

The argument is the `ModuleCat` form of the abelian one in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.LocallyConstantAbelian.Morphisms`, and the two
ingredients which make it work are the same. Restriction along a morphism of the site commutes
with sheafification, hence carries a constant sheaf to the constant sheaf on the same module
(`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSheafOverMapIso`, which is stated for an arbitrary coefficient
category), so a trivialization survives refinement and two locally constant sheaves can be
trivialized over one object at once. With both sheaves trivialized over an object `V`, the map `φ`
becomes a map `ψ : A̲ ⟶ B̲` of constant sheaves; since `A` is of finite type it is generated by
finitely many elements, whose images are *locally* in the image of the constant section map
(`Stacks.Sheafification.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify_moduleCat` and
`Stacks.Sheafification.exists_cover_representatives`), so after one refinement the generators lift
to elements of `B`. Their relations then have to be checked in `B` itself, which needs the constant
section map to be injective, and in general it is not. Passing to the quotient of `B` by the kernel
of that map repairs this without changing the sheaf `B̲`, by
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.isIso_constantSheaf_map_constantQuotientModuleMk`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_smallSite` —
  Stacks 093S (3) on a small site with the modules in the site's own universe, which is the
  source's setting; this is the form the tag is registered on, and it has no hypothesis the source
  does not state.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules` — the same over a site
  of unrelated universes, which needs the Kan extensions of the implementation notes as an input.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_of_hasPullbacks` —
  the same on a site with pullbacks, where no hypothesis relates the module universe to the
  universes of the site.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_isConstantModuleMapAt` — the local form, from one pair of
  trivializations over one object.

## Implementation notes

**Which declarations carry 093S.** Tag 093S has three parts — sheaves of sets, sheaves of abelian
groups, and sheaves of modules over a fixed ring — and the repo convention for a multi-part tag is
suffixed attributes with no bare one. Part (1) is
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map` with `@[stacks 093S "sets"]`,
part (2) is `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_abelian_smallSite`,
and part (3) is
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_smallSite` below. The
general-site forms of parts (2) and (3) keep their own attributes, so both are registered; the
small-site forms are the ones that assume nothing the source does not.

**The ambient category.** Definition 093O takes `F` to be "a sheaf of sets, groups, abelian
groups, rings, modules over a fixed ring `Λ`, etc." — a sheaf *valued* in the category of such
objects — and the constant sheaf `M̲` to be the sheafification of the presheaf `U ↦ M`. The ambient
category of part (3), written `Mod(C, Λ)` in the source, is therefore `Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} R)`,
exactly parallel to parts (1) and (2); no equivalence of categories with `SheafOfModules Λ̲` is
involved. Reading part (3) as a statement phrased in `SheafOfModules` would be wrong. The library
already reads the section this way on other registered statements: the sibling lemma 093U (3), a
weak Serre subcategory of the same `Mod(C, Λ)`, and 095C (3), the small-étale-site specialization
of part (3), which is registered on a direct corollary of the declaration below.

The finite-type hypothesis on the source is `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.IsFiniteTypeLocallyConstant`,
local constancy with finitely generated constant values, where the source says "of finite type".
For a *locally constant* sheaf the two agree: over an object whose empty sieve is not covering they
agree by Tag 093N (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.constantModuleSheaf_isFiniteType_iff`), and over
an object whose empty sieve *is* covering both hold, the empty family being a covering family
there. Finitely generated constant values is also the form the proof uses, and it keeps the three
parts of 093S uniform: each is stated for a `Sheaf J D` with `D` the coefficient category, together
with local constancy of both sheaves and a finiteness condition on the values of the source. It is
also the form the rest of the library registers this notion in — Tags 03RW (3), 093U (3) and
095C (3) all carry it — and the attribute below names it, so the reading is on the record rather
than hidden.

As in part (2), the statement is proved over an *arbitrary* object of the site rather than only
over a final object, which is how the source phrases it; the version over a final object is the
special case. No finality hypothesis on the site is used.

**The one input beyond the ones Stacks 093S (3) states**, which the engine lemma over a site of
unrelated universes takes as a hypothesis, is the family of pointwise right Kan extensions along
`(Over.map t).op` out of which `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSheafOverMapIso` — a trivialization
survives refinement — is built. It is a limit-existence condition on the coefficient category: the
index category of each of those limits is `StructuredArrow _ (Over.map t).op`, of the size of the
site.

On a small site it is therefore not a hypothesis at all but a theorem. For `C : Type u` with
`SmallCategory C` and the modules taken in the same universe, those index categories are `u`-small,
so `ModuleCat.hasLimitsOfShape` produces every one of the limits, and
`CategoryTheory.HasWeakSheafify` on each localized site comes out the same way. That is
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_smallSite`, which carries
the part (3) attribute: a small site with coefficients in its own universe is the source's setting,
and this library's convention for a small site, so nothing there is assumed that the source does
not assume.

Two other conditions supply the same input over a site of unrelated universes, and neither implies
the other: `UnivLE.{max u v, w}`, which gives limits of the size of the site in `ModuleCat.{w} R`;
and `Limits.HasPullbacks C`, under which `Over.map t` is a left adjoint and the index category of
each of those limits has an initial object
(`Stacks.Localization.hasPointwiseRightKanExtension_overMapOp`), giving
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_of_hasPullbacks`. Both are
kept unchanged for callers that already hold them; neither is needed to register the tag. The
second place the universes used to enter, the local surjectivity of sheafification for presheaves
of modules, no longer needs them at all: see
`Stacks.Sheafification.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify_moduleCat`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 093S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093S)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe w r v u

namespace Stacks.ConstantSheaf

variable {R : Type r} [Ring R]

/-- Values on a generating family of a module which respect every relation of that family descend
to a homomorphism. -/
lemma exists_hom_of_moduleGeneratorImages {A B : ModuleCat.{w} R} (n : ℕ) (z : Fin n → A)
    (hz : Function.Surjective (Finsupp.linearCombination R z)) (b : Fin n → B)
    (hrel : ∀ x : Fin n →₀ R, Finsupp.linearCombination R z x = 0 →
      Finsupp.linearCombination R b x = 0) :
    ∃ g : A ⟶ B, ∀ i, g (z i) = b i := by
  let p := Finsupp.linearCombination R z
  let q := Finsupp.linearCombination R b
  have hpq : LinearMap.ker p ≤ LinearMap.ker q := fun x hx => hrel x (LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hx)
  let ε := p.quotKerEquivOfSurjective hz
  refine ⟨ModuleCat.ofHom (((LinearMap.ker p).liftQ q hpq).comp ε.symm.toLinearMap), fun i => ?_⟩
  have heq : ε.symm (z i) = Submodule.Quotient.mk (Finsupp.single i (1 : R)) := by
    apply ε.injective
    simp [ε, p, Finsupp.linearCombination_single]
  show ((LinearMap.ker p).liftQ q hpq) (ε.symm (z i)) = b i
  rw [heq]
  calc ((LinearMap.ker p).liftQ q hpq) (Submodule.Quotient.mk (Finsupp.single i (1 : R)))
      = q (Finsupp.single i 1) := DFunLike.congr_fun (Submodule.liftQ_mkQ (LinearMap.ker p) q hpq) _
    _ = b i := by simp [q, Finsupp.linearCombination_single]

/-- Values on a generating family which an injective homomorphism makes compatible with the
generators descend to a homomorphism. -/
lemma exists_hom_of_moduleGeneratorImages_of_injective {A B D : ModuleCat.{w} R} (n : ℕ)
    (z : Fin n → A) (hz : Function.Surjective (Finsupp.linearCombination R z)) (b : Fin n → B)
    (f : A ⟶ D) (g : B ⟶ D) (hg : Function.Injective g) (h : ∀ j, g (b j) = f (z j)) :
    ∃ gh : A ⟶ B, ∀ i, gh (z i) = b i := by
  refine exists_hom_of_moduleGeneratorImages n z hz b fun x hx => hg ?_
  rw [map_zero]
  calc g (Finsupp.linearCombination R b x)
      = Finsupp.linearCombination R (fun j => g (b j)) x :=
        Finsupp.apply_linearCombination R g.hom b x
    _ = Finsupp.linearCombination R (fun j => f (z j)) x := by simp only [h]
    _ = f (Finsupp.linearCombination R z x) :=
        (Finsupp.apply_linearCombination R f.hom z x).symm
    _ = 0 := by rw [hx, map_zero]

/-- A finitely generated module is generated, as an `R`-module, by a finite family indexed by
`Fin n`. -/
lemma exists_fin_generators_of_isFG (A : ModuleCat.{w} R) (hA : ModuleCat.isFG R A) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (z : Fin n → A), Function.Surjective (Finsupp.linearCombination R z) := by
  have : Module.Finite R A := (ModuleCat.isFG_iff A).mp hA
  obtain ⟨n, z, hz⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin (R := R) (M := A)
  refine ⟨n, z, ?_⟩
  rw [← LinearMap.range_eq_top, Finsupp.range_linearCombination, hz]

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (K : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [HasWeakSheafify K (ModuleCat.{w} R)]

/-- Two maps out of a constant sheaf of modules which agree on the constant sections of a
generating family, over a final object, are equal. -/
lemma constantSheaf_hom_ext_of_moduleGenerators {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (A : ModuleCat.{w} R)
    (Q : Sheaf K (ModuleCat.{w} R)) (n : ℕ) (z : Fin n → A)
    (hz : Function.Surjective (Finsupp.linearCombination R z))
    (a b : (constantSheaf K (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ⟶ Q)
    (h : ∀ i, a.hom.app (op T)
        ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj A)).app (op T) (z i)) =
      b.hom.app (op T)
        ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj A)).app (op T) (z i))) :
    a = b := by
  let η := CategoryTheory.toSheafify K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj A)
  let a' := η ≫ a.hom
  let b' := η ≫ b.hom
  have he : a'.app (op T) = b'.app (op T) :=
    ModuleCat.hom_ext <| LinearMap.ext_on_range (by
      rw [← Finsupp.range_linearCombination, LinearMap.range_eq_top.mpr hz]) h
  apply Sheaf.hom_ext
  apply sheafify_hom_ext K _ _ Q.property
  show a' = b'
  apply NatTrans.ext
  funext V
  have ha := a'.naturality (hT.from V.unop).op
  have hb := b'.naturality (hT.from V.unop).op
  rw [he] at ha
  have hh := ha.trans hb.symm
  change (𝟙 A) ≫ a'.app V = (𝟙 A) ≫ b'.app V at hh
  simpa only [Category.id_comp] using hh

/-- A map of constant sheaves of modules which, over a final object, carries the constant sections
of a generating family to constant sections is, after projecting onto the constant quotient, the
map of constant sheaves associated to a homomorphism. -/
lemma exists_constantSheaf_map_eq_comp_constantQuotientModuleMk {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R)
    (χ : (constantSheaf K (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ⟶ (constantSheaf K (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B)
    (n : ℕ) (z : Fin n → A) (hz : Function.Surjective (Finsupp.linearCombination R z))
    (b : Fin n → B)
    (hb : ∀ j, (CategoryTheory.toSheafify K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj B)).app (op T) (b j) =
      χ.hom.app (op T)
        ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj A)).app (op T) (z j))) :
    ∃ g : A ⟶ constantQuotientModule K T B, (constantSheaf K (ModuleCat.{w} R)).map g =
      χ ≫ (constantSheaf K (ModuleCat.{w} R)).map (constantQuotientModuleMk K T B) := by
  set pr := constantQuotientModuleMk K T B
  set ηA := CategoryTheory.toSheafify K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj A)
  set ηBq := CategoryTheory.toSheafify K
    ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj (constantQuotientModule K T B))
  set cpr := (constantSheaf K (ModuleCat.{w} R)).map pr
  have hnat : ∀ y : B, ηBq.app (op T) (pr y) = cpr.hom.app (op T)
      ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).obj B)).app (op T) y) := fun y =>
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (NatTrans.congr_app
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify_naturality K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).map pr)) (op T)) y
  have hfz : ∀ j, ηBq.app (op T) (pr (b j)) =
      (ηA.app (op T) ≫ χ.hom.app (op T) ≫ cpr.hom.app (op T)) (z j) := by
    intro j
    rw [hnat (b j), hb j]
    rfl
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_hom_of_moduleGeneratorImages_of_injective n z hz (fun j => pr (b j))
    (ηA.app (op T) ≫ χ.hom.app (op T) ≫ cpr.hom.app (op T)) (ηBq.app (op T))
    (injective_constantSection_constantQuotientModule K hT B) hfz
  refine ⟨g, constantSheaf_hom_ext_of_moduleGenerators K hT A _ n z hz _ _ fun j => ?_⟩
  have hg₁ := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (NatTrans.congr_app
    (CategoryTheory.toSheafify_naturality K ((Functor.const Cᵒᵖ).map g)) (op T)) (z j)
  change ηBq.app (op T) (g (z j)) =
    ((constantSheaf K (ModuleCat.{w} R)).map g).hom.app (op T) (ηA.app (op T) (z j)) at hg₁
  rw [← hg₁, hg j]
  exact hfz j

end Stacks.ConstantSheaf

namespace Stacks.ConstantSheaf

variable {R : Type r} [Ring R] {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [∀ U : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)]

/-- The conclusion of Tag 093S (3) over one object of the site: the restricted morphism is the map
of constant sheaves of modules associated to a homomorphism of modules, with finitely generated
source value. -/
abbrev IsConstantModuleMapAt (F G : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} R)) (φ : F ⟶ G) (V : C) : Prop :=
  ∃ (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R), ModuleCat.isFG R A ∧
    ∃ (g : A ⟶ B)
      (eF : (constantSheaf (J.over V) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ≅
        (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) V).obj F)
      (eG : (constantSheaf (J.over V) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B ≅
        (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) V).obj G),
      (constantSheaf (J.over V) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).map g ≫ eG.hom =
        eF.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) V).map φ

section OverMap

variable {U V : C} (t : V ⟶ U)
  [∀ F : (Over V)ᵒᵖ ⥤ ModuleCat.{w} R, (Over.map t).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension F]

/-- The restriction along `Over.map t` of a map of constant sheaves of modules on `Over U`, read
as a map of constant sheaves of modules on `Over V`. -/
def constantModuleMapRestrict (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R)
    (ψ : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ⟶
      (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B) :
    (constantSheaf (J.over V) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ⟶
      (constantSheaf (J.over V) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B :=
  (constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t A).hom ≫
    (J.overMapPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) t).map ψ ≫
      (constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t B).inv

/-- **A trivialization survives refinement.** If a sheaf of modules becomes constant with value `E`
after restriction to `U`, it becomes constant with the *same* value `E` after restriction to any
`V` lying over `U`. -/
def overPullbackIsoOfMapModule (F : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} R)) (E : ModuleCat.{w} R)
    (e : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).obj F) :
    (constantSheaf (J.over V) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) V).obj F :=
  constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t E ≪≫
    (J.overMapPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) t).mapIso e

/-- The forward map of `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.overPullbackIsoOfMapModule`, unfolded. -/
lemma overPullbackIsoOfMapModule_hom (F : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} R)) (E : ModuleCat.{w} R)
    (e : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj E ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).obj F) :
    (overPullbackIsoOfMapModule J t F E e).hom =
      (constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t E).hom ≫
        (J.overMapPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) t).map e.hom :=
  rfl

/-- The restricted map is compatible with the two restriction isomorphisms. -/
lemma constantModuleMapRestrict_comp (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R)
    (ψ : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ⟶
      (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B) :
    constantModuleMapRestrict J t A B ψ ≫ (constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t B).hom =
      (constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t A).hom ≫
        (J.overMapPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) t).map ψ := by
  simp [constantModuleMapRestrict]

/-- A constant section of the restricted sheaf on `Over V` which, read on `Over U`, represents the
image of a constant section of `A̲` represents it already on `Over V`. -/
lemma constantModuleMapRestrict_section (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R)
    (ψ : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ⟶
      (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B)
    (a : A) (b : B)
    (h : (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U)
          ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj B)).app (op (Over.mk t)) b =
      ψ.hom.app (op (Over.mk t)) ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U)
        ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj A)).app (op (Over.mk t)) a)) :
    (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over V)
        ((Functor.const (Over V)ᵒᵖ).obj B)).app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V))) b =
      (constantModuleMapRestrict J t A B ψ).hom.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V)))
        ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over V)
          ((Functor.const (Over V)ᵒᵖ).obj A)).app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V))) a) := by
  set Ti : (Over V)ᵒᵖ := op (Over.mk (𝟙 V))
  set oA := constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t A
  set oB := constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t B
  apply (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (oB.hom.hom.app Ti)).injective
  have hunit : ∀ (E : ModuleCat.{w} R) (x : E),
      (constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t E).hom.hom.app Ti
        ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over V) ((Functor.const (Over V)ᵒᵖ).obj E)).app Ti x) =
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U)
        ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj E)).app ((Over.map t).op.obj Ti) x := fun E x =>
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
      (NatTrans.congr_app (constantSheafOverMapIso_unit J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t E) Ti) x
  have hcomp := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (NatTrans.congr_app
      (Sheaf.hom_ext_iff.mp (constantModuleMapRestrict_comp J t A B ψ)) Ti)
    ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over V) ((Functor.const (Over V)ᵒᵖ).obj A)).app Ti a)
  change oB.hom.hom.app Ti
      ((constantModuleMapRestrict J t A B ψ).hom.app Ti
        ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over V)
          ((Functor.const (Over V)ᵒᵖ).obj A)).app Ti a)) =
    ψ.hom.app ((Over.map t).op.obj Ti) (oA.hom.hom.app Ti
      ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over V)
        ((Functor.const (Over V)ᵒᵖ).obj A)).app Ti a)) at hcomp
  rw [hunit B b, hcomp, hunit A a]
  let P (Z : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) : Prop :=
    (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U) ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj B)).app Z b =
      ψ.hom.app Z ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U)
        ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj A)).app Z a)
  exact (congrArg P (overMap_op_obj_mkId t)).mpr h

end OverMap

section Engine

variable [∀ (X Y : C) (t : X ⟶ Y) (E : (Over X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ ModuleCat.{w} R),
  (Over.map t).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension E]

/-- Constant sections of `B` representing, over `V`, the images under a map `ψ` of constant sheaves
of the constant sections of a generating family of `A` make the restriction of `φ` to `V` a map of
constant sheaves of modules. -/
lemma isConstantModuleMapAt_of_constantSection_representatives (F G : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} R))
    (φ : F ⟶ G) {U V : C} (t : V ⟶ U) (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R) (hA : ModuleCat.isFG R A)
    (eF : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).obj F)
    (eG : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).obj G)
    (ψ : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ⟶
      (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B)
    (hψ : ψ ≫ eG.hom = eF.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).map φ)
    (n : ℕ) (z : Fin n → A) (hz : Function.Surjective (Finsupp.linearCombination R z))
    (b : Fin n → B)
    (hb : ∀ j, (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U)
          ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj B)).app (op (Over.mk t)) (b j) =
      ψ.hom.app (op (Over.mk t)) ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U)
        ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj A)).app (op (Over.mk t)) (z j))) :
    IsConstantModuleMapAt J F G φ V := by
  have hT : IsTerminal (Over.mk (𝟙 V)) := Over.mkIdTerminal
  have hprIso := isIso_constantSheaf_map_constantQuotientModuleMk (J.over V) hT B
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_constantSheaf_map_eq_comp_constantQuotientModuleMk (J.over V) hT A B
    (constantModuleMapRestrict J t A B ψ) n z hz b fun j =>
      constantModuleMapRestrict_section J t A B ψ (z j) (b j) (hb j)
  have hsq : constantModuleMapRestrict J t A B ψ ≫
        (overPullbackIsoOfMapModule J t G B eG).hom =
      (overPullbackIsoOfMapModule J t F A eF).hom ≫
        (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) V).map φ := by
    show constantModuleMapRestrict J t A B ψ ≫
        (constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t B).hom ≫
          (J.overMapPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) t).map eG.hom =
      ((constantSheafOverMapIso J (ModuleCat.{w} R) t A).hom ≫
          (J.overMapPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) t).map eF.hom) ≫
        (J.overMapPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) t).map
          ((J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).map φ)
    rw [← Category.assoc, constantModuleMapRestrict_comp J t A B ψ, Category.assoc,
      ← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, hψ, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc]
  refine ⟨A, constantQuotientModule (J.over V) (Over.mk (𝟙 V)) B, hA, g,
    overPullbackIsoOfMapModule J t F A eF, (asIso ((constantSheaf (J.over V) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).map
      (constantQuotientModuleMk (J.over V) (Over.mk (𝟙 V)) B))).symm ≪≫
        overPullbackIsoOfMapModule J t G B eG, ?_⟩
  rw [hg]
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, asIso_inv, Category.assoc, IsIso.hom_inv_id_assoc]
  exact hsq

/-- **Stacks 093S (3), from one pair of trivializations.** Given trivializations of `F` and of `G`
over the same object `U`, the value of `F` being finitely generated, there is a covering of `U` on
each member of which the restriction of `φ` is the map of constant sheaves of modules associated to
a homomorphism of modules. -/
lemma exists_cover_isConstantModuleMapAt (F G : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} R)) (φ : F ⟶ G) (U : C)
    (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R) (hA : ModuleCat.isFG R A)
    (eF : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).obj F)
    (eG : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B ≅
      (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).obj G) :
    ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (X : I → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ ∀ i, IsConstantModuleMapAt J F G φ (X i) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, z, hz⟩ := exists_fin_generators_of_isFG A hA
  set ψ : (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ⟶
      (constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B :=
    eF.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).map φ ≫ eG.inv with hψdef
  have hψ : ψ ≫ eG.hom = eF.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) U).map φ := by
    simp [hψdef]
  set ηA := CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U) ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj A)
  set ηB := CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U) ((Functor.const (Over U)ᵒᵖ).obj B)
  set T : Over U := Over.mk (𝟙 U)
  obtain ⟨I, W, k, hk, hm⟩ := Stacks.Sheafification.exists_cover_representatives (J.over U) ηB T
    (fun j => ψ.hom.app (op T) (ηA.app (op T) (z j)))
  refine ⟨I, fun i => (W i).left, fun i => (W i).hom, ?_, fun i => ?_⟩
  · rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff, Sieve.overEquiv_ofArrows] at hk
    change Sieve.ofArrows (fun i => (W i).left) (fun i => (k i).left) ∈ J U at hk
    have hleft : (fun i => (W i).hom) = fun i => (k i).left := by
      funext i
      exact ((Category.comp_id ((k i).left)).symm.trans (Over.w (k i))).symm
    rwa [hleft]
  · obtain ⟨-, hrep⟩ := hm i
    choose b hb using hrep
    refine isConstantModuleMapAt_of_constantSection_representatives J F G φ (W i).hom A B hA eF eG
      ψ hψ n z hz b fun j => ?_
    have h₁ := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (ηA.naturality (k i).op) (z j)
    have h₂ := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (ψ.hom.naturality (k i).op) (ηA.app (op T) (z j))
    change ηA.app (op (W i)) (z j) =
      ((constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A).obj.map (k i).op
        (ηA.app (op T) (z j)) at h₁
    change ψ.hom.app (op (W i))
        (((constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A).obj.map (k i).op
          (ηA.app (op T) (z j))) =
      ((constantSheaf (J.over U) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B).obj.map (k i).op
        (ψ.hom.app (op T) (ηA.app (op T) (z j))) at h₂
    show ηB.app (op (W i)) (b j) = ψ.hom.app (op (W i)) (ηA.app (op (W i)) (z j))
    rw [h₁, h₂]
    exact (hb j).symm

/-- **Stacks 093S (3).** A morphism of locally constant sheaves of `R`-modules whose source is
locally constant of finite type is, on a covering of any object, obtained from a homomorphism of
`R`-modules.

Carries one hypothesis the source does not state: the family of pointwise right Kan extensions
along `(Over.map t).op` out of which `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSheafOverMapIso` is built. It is
a limit-existence side condition on the coefficient category, implied both by `UnivLE.{max u v, w}`
and by fibre products in the site; see this file's implementation notes, and
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_of_hasPullbacks` for the
form carrying no universe condition at all.
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_smallSite` is the form on
a small site, where that side condition is a theorem rather than a hypothesis, and is what part (3)
of the tag is registered on. -/
@[stacks 093S "part (3), sheaves of Λ-modules, with `of finite type` in the equivalent \
  locally-constant-with-finitely-generated-values form of Tag 093N; assumes pointwise right Kan \
  extensions along the localization functors, a limit-existence side condition implied by fibre \
  products in the site", sga "4 IX 2.1"]
lemma exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules
    (F G : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} R)) (φ : F ⟶ G)
    (hF : IsFiniteTypeLocallyConstant R J F) [hG : IsLocallyConstant J G] (U : C) :
    ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (X : I → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ ∀ i,
        ∃ (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R), ModuleCat.isFG R A ∧
          ∃ (g : A ⟶ B)
            (eF : (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ≅
              (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) (X i)).obj F)
            (eG : (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B ≅
              (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) (X i)).obj G),
              (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).map g ≫ eG.hom =
                eF.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) (X i)).map φ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨I, Y, f, hf, hGc⟩ := hG.exists_cover U
  refine exists_cover_trans J (P := IsConstantModuleMapAt J F G φ) hf fun i => ?_
  obtain ⟨B, ⟨eB⟩⟩ := (hGc i).mem_essImage
  obtain ⟨I', Z, g, hg, hFc⟩ := hF (Y i)
  refine exists_cover_trans J (P := IsConstantModuleMapAt J F G φ) hg fun j => ?_
  obtain ⟨A, hA, ⟨eA⟩⟩ := hFc j
  exact exists_cover_isConstantModuleMapAt J F G φ (Z j) A B hA eA
    (overPullbackIsoOfMapModule J (g j) G B eB)

end Engine

/-- **The same statement on a site with pullbacks, with no hypothesis relating the module universe
to the universes of the site.** The Kan extension instances which
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules` assumes are supplied by
`Stacks.Localization.hasPointwiseRightKanExtension_overMapOp`, since `Over.map t` is then a left
adjoint. This is the form the étale sites of chapter 59 use: a small étale site has fibre products,
while nothing there relates the coefficient universe to the site. -/
lemma exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_of_hasPullbacks [HasPullbacks C]
    (F G : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} R)) (φ : F ⟶ G)
    (hF : IsFiniteTypeLocallyConstant R J F) [IsLocallyConstant J G] (U : C) :
    ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (X : I → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ ∀ i,
        ∃ (A B : ModuleCat.{w} R), ModuleCat.isFG R A ∧
          ∃ (g : A ⟶ B)
            (eF : (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj A ≅
              (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) (X i)).obj F)
            (eG : (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).obj B ≅
              (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) (X i)).obj G),
              (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{w} R)).map g ≫ eG.hom =
                eF.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{w} R) (X i)).map φ :=
  have : ∀ (X Y : C) (t : X ⟶ Y) (E : (Over X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ ModuleCat.{w} R),
      (Over.map t).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension E := fun _ _ t E =>
    Stacks.Localization.hasPointwiseRightKanExtension_overMapOp t (ModuleCat.{w} R) E
  exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules J F G φ hF U

section SmallSite

/-- **Stacks 093S (3).** A morphism of locally constant sheaves of `R`-modules whose source is
locally constant of finite type is, on a covering of any object, obtained from a homomorphism of
`R`-modules.

Stated on a small site, `C : Type u` with `SmallCategory C` and the modules in the same universe,
which is the setting of the source and this library's convention for a small site. In it the
statement carries *no* hypothesis beyond the source's: the pointwise right Kan extensions along the
localization functors `(Over.map t).op`, which
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules` takes as an input, are
limits over `u`-small index categories and so exist in `ModuleCat.{u} R` by
`ModuleCat.hasLimitsOfShape`; sheafification on each localized site is automatic for the same
reason. Neither `UnivLE` nor fibre products in the site are needed. -/
@[stacks 093S "part (3), sheaves of Λ-modules, with `of finite type` in the equivalent \
  locally-constant-with-finitely-generated-values form of Tag 093N", sga "4 IX 2.1"]
lemma exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules_smallSite
    {R : Type r} [Ring R] {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    (F G : Sheaf J (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (φ : F ⟶ G)
    (hF : IsFiniteTypeLocallyConstant R J F) [IsLocallyConstant J G] (U : C) :
    ∃ (I : Type u) (X : I → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ ∀ i,
        ∃ (A B : ModuleCat.{u} R), ModuleCat.isFG R A ∧
          ∃ (g : A ⟶ B)
            (eF : (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj A ≅
              (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{u} R) (X i)).obj F)
            (eG : (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{u} R)).obj B ≅
              (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{u} R) (X i)).obj G),
              (constantSheaf (J.over (X i)) (ModuleCat.{u} R)).map g ≫ eG.hom =
                eF.hom ≫ (J.overPullback (ModuleCat.{u} R) (X i)).map φ :=
  have : ∀ (X Y : C) (t : X ⟶ Y) (E : (Over X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} R),
      (Over.map t).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension E :=
    fun _ _ _ _ _ => ModuleCat.hasLimitsOfShape.has_limit _
  exists_cover_restrict_eq_constantSheaf_map_modules J F G φ hF U

end SmallSite

end Stacks.ConstantSheaf

